  "authoringNote": "C09 R05 regression. R05 is order-centred: every current usable order needs a linked receipt, meaning a current usable receipt that references that exact order version and states a receipt time. A is linked by receipt 1, which follows the span end 2026-09-02T12:00Z. B has no link: receipt 2 states no time, receipt 3 references B version 2 (not B v1, and not supplied), and receipt 4 failed provenance (its held bytes do not match contentHash, which is a deliberately different digest), so no link is read from its body. R05.order_receipt_missing names B (missing, authorization coordinator, needs_information); A's good receipt does not hide it. Usable receipts exist, so receipt 4 is not a candidate and no receipt_failed_provenance or no_usable_receipt holds. R09 reports receipt 4 with hash_mismatch (conflict, administrative reviewer, needs_human_review), parent set receipt 4. Receipt 4 is bound by metadata only and never cited. Unlinked usable receipts are still cited (C05, C09): R05 cites receipt 1 (three), receipt 2 (document ID and version; no time), receipt 3 (three) and both order dates (ten). R02 twelve (receipts 1 to 3, encounter, both orders); R03 eighteen (both orders complete and equal: pass); R04 nine (pass); R01 nine; R06 five; R07 one. State needs_human_review.",
